# =============================================================================
# Python artifacts
# Byte-compiled caches, linter caches, packaging metadata, virtualenvs.
# pyproject.toml at the root is real config and stays tracked - it is not
# matched by any pattern below.
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# =============================================================================
# Test temp root
# Every throwaway git repository and lock sandbox the suite builds (see
# .claude/tools/tests/tmproot.py). Anchored with a leading slash so it is the
# project root's tmp/ and nothing else. Before task-0069 these artifacts were
# written under the host temp directory, where no check this project runs could
# see them - twelve supervisor locks and nineteen directories accumulated in
# the user profile unreported.
/tmp/

# =============================================================================
# Codegraph index
# Per-machine code knowledge graph built by the codegraph CLI.
# =============================================================================
.codegraph/

# =============================================================================
# Pipeline runtime state
# SQLite run state and other per-machine pipeline artifacts.
# =============================================================================
.agentry/state/

# =============================================================================
# Per-machine local settings
# May hold personal tokens or paths; never shared across machines.
# =============================================================================
.claude/settings.local.json

# =============================================================================
# Project work product (plans, specs, tasks, memory)
# These are generated while running a project through the pipeline and do not
# belong in the published template. Only the scaffolding a fresh clone needs
# (templates, contract docs, and the directory skeleton) is kept - see the
# negations below. Contents are excluded rather than the directory itself, so
# the negations can re-include specific files inside.
# =============================================================================
.agentry/plans/
.agentry/specs/*
.agentry/memory/*
.agentry/project/*

# Memory store contract survives for a fresh clone; memory.db itself (and any
# --export markdown beside it) is one project's internals and stays out.
!.agentry/memory/README.md

# Spec template survives for a fresh clone, same scaffolding role as
# .agentry/tasks/templates/.
!.agentry/specs/_template.md

# Project overlay contract, and every overlay document, survive for a fresh
# clone: rules/self-learning.md sends agents here to record project quirks, so a
# newly created .agentry/project/quirks.md must be tracked, not silently dropped.
# Markdown only - anything else under the overlay stays excluded.
!.agentry/project/*.md

# Task work product is excluded per-folder (not via .agentry/tasks/) so the
# templates/ folder and the pipeline's directory skeleton stay tracked.
.agentry/tasks/backlog/*
.agentry/tasks/active/*
.agentry/tasks/done/*
.agentry/tasks/epics/*
.agentry/tasks/handoffs/*

# Keep the empty-directory placeholders so git tracks the skeleton itself.
!.agentry/tasks/backlog/.gitkeep
!.agentry/tasks/active/.gitkeep
!.agentry/tasks/done/.gitkeep
!.agentry/tasks/epics/.gitkeep
!.agentry/tasks/handoffs/.gitkeep
